  "reason": "The records provide complementary but disconnected guidance. R2, R4, and R18 show that pressure, including combined high pressure and temperature, can drive persistent structural transformations in HEAs, while R7 shows that energetic processing can transform and refine AlCoCrFeNi specifically. R3 and R12 closely anticipate the coherent-interface mechanism—dislocation transmission, stress-concentration relief, and suppression of cracking—and R1, R5, R10, and R14 support the value of multiple deformation mechanisms. However, no record applies HPHT to the eutectic Al0.7CoCrFeNi lamellar FCC/B2 alloy or predicts that it will generate the particular hierarchical coherent-interface architecture. Combining these strands points in the right direction, but selecting the specific HPHT treatment and obtaining that architecture would require a substantial new idea."
